cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fairfig for figures in a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "fairfig: colour-blind-safe, journal-ready matplotlib figures"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A matplotlib style and helper library that gives scientific figures one consistent,
  colour-blind-safe visual identity: Okabe-Ito hues ordered for colour-vision deficiency
  and set at distinct brightness levels (tested with a colour-blind reader), batlow and
  vik colour maps for ordered data, exact column widths for ACS, Elsevier and Nature,
  markers for experiment and lines for models, a bundled monospace font, SVG and PDF
  export, and built-in colour-blind and greyscale checks.
